Now we need to achieve goal.

Let's design plan:

Phase A: Prepare origin and destination availabilities.

1. Detach task profile from shift_candidate_alpha to free route_task_profile_alpha.
   (detach_task_profile shift_candidate_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Now route_task_profile_alpha available.

2. Attach task profile to origin_availability_alpha.
   (attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

3. Attach task profile to destination_availability_alpha.
   (attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Now origin and destination have task profile linked.

4. Allocate vehicle to destination_availability_alpha (vehicle_unit_beta) (since we need vehicle allocated there).
   (allocate_vehicle_unit destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta)

Check preconditions: candidate_created destination_availability_alpha (yes), not vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (currently false), vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta (yes). Effect: vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha true, candidate_vehicle_linked destination_availability_alpha vehicle_unit_beta, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_beta becomes false.

Now we have destination_availability_alpha vehicle allocated.

5. Confirm preparedness for origin_availability_alpha.
   Need candidate_created origin_availability_alpha (yes), vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha (yes), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (yes after attach), not candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (currently false). So we can do:
   (confirm_candidate_preparedness origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Effect: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha true.

6. Confirm preparedness for destination_availability_alpha.
   Preconditions: candidate_created destination_availability_alpha (yes), vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (yes after allocate), candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (yes), not candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha (currently false). So:
   (confirm_candidate_preparedness destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Effect: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha true.

Now origin and destination are prepared.

Now we need to activate origin and destination nodes (make ready) before loading payloads.

7. Activate origin node:
   Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (yes), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (yes), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (yes), not origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha (currently false), not origin_node_occupied origin_node_alpha (currently false). So:
   (activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Effect: origin_node_ready true.

8. Activate destination node:
   Preconditions: candidate_prepared destination_availability_alpha (yes), candidate_task_profile_linked destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (yes), destination_availability_node_linked destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha (yes), not destination_node_ready destination_node_alpha (false), not destination_node_occupied destination_node_alpha (false). So:
   (activate_destination_node destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)

Effect: destination_node_ready true.

Now we need to load payloads onto origin and destination (to get nodes occupied and availability locked etc). Goal requires origin_node_occupied and destination_node_occupied, also origin_availability_locked, destination_availability_locked, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed.

We need to load origin payload then lock origin availability; load destination payload then lock destination availability.

But lock action requires candidate_prepared, candidate_operator_linked, origin_availability_node_linked, origin_node_ready, not origin_availability_locked. So we need operator linked to origin_availability_alpha. Currently origin_availability_alpha has no operator linked. We need to assign operator resource to origin_availability_alpha.

Similarly for destination.

We have operator resource driver_operator_alpha. It is currently linked to shift_candidate_alpha. We need to free it to link to origin and destination. We can release operator from shift_candidate_alpha via release_operator_resource (requires candidate_operator_linked ?candidate ?operator_resource). After release, operator becomes available.

Thus:

9. Release operator from shift_candidate_alpha.
   (release_operator_resource shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Effect: operator_available driver_operator_alpha true, candidate_operator_linked shift_candidate_alpha driver_operator_alpha removed.

Now operator available.

10. Assign operator to origin_availability_alpha.
    Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (yes), operator_available driver_operator_alpha (yes). So:
    (assign_operator_resource origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Effect: candidate_operator_linked origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha true, operator_available driver_operator_alpha false.

Now we can lock origin availability.

11. Lock origin availability:
    Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (yes), candidate_operator_linked origin_availability_alpha driver_operator_alpha (yes), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (yes), origin_node_ready origin_node_alpha (yes after activate), not origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha (currently false). So:
    (lock_origin_availability origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha driver_operator_alpha)

Effect: origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true.

Now origin availability locked and confirmed.

Now load origin payload:

12. Load origin payload:
    Preconditions: candidate_prepared origin_availability_alpha (yes), origin_availability_node_linked origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha (yes), cargo_available cargo_payload_alpha (yes), not origin_availability_locked origin_availability_alpha? Wait load_origin_payload precondition includes not origin_availability_locked ?origin_availability. Actually load_origin_payload requires NOT origin_availability_locked. But after lock, origin_availability_locked is true, so we cannot load payload after lock. Indeed load_origin_payload requires not origin_availability_locked. So we need to load payload before locking. Similarly for destination.

